ic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.09872103996498471,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":79.5,"_gate_rev_durability":0.13239636175881841,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":91.2,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.1938172898521973,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.06856341891194484,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":100.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.02785276282812669,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":53.6,"_gate_insider_own":0.06365,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":42.4,"_gate_insider_buying":0.647,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":64.7,"pf":[],"description_full":"The Bancorp, Inc. operates as the financial holding company for The Bancorp Bank, National Association that provides banking products and services in the United States. It offers a range of deposit products and services, including checking, savings, money market, and commercial accounts. The company also provides securities-backed lines of credit and insurance policy cash value-backed lines of credit; investor advisor financing; financing to investment advisors; Small Business Administration loan; lease financing for commercial and government vehicle fleets; commercial real estate bridge loans, as well as consumer fintech loans comprising short-term extensions of credit, including secured credit card loans, payroll advances, and others. In addition, it offers automated clearing house (ACH) bill, and other payment services; debit and prepaid card issuing services; card and bill payment; account services; data processing services, check imaging, loan processing, electronic bill payment and statement rendering; call center customer support; access to automated teller machine networks; bank accounting and general ledger system; data warehousing services; and software development services. The company was incorporated in 1999 and is headquartered in Wilmington, Delaware.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Damian M. Kozlowski | CEO, President & Director | Age 60 | Compensation: $1.0M (FY2022)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 733 people. Revenue per employee of $960K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 14%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $352K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $27K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["The Bancorp, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $1.9B market cap on $704M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +26% over the past three years and +13% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +2.2pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 58% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 48-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $258M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 37 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.16\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 1.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 19.4% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 6.4% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 1.7\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.5) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (14.6% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 14% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 62% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Insiders are net buyers (65% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Financial Services peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Growing faster than most Financial Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Precision Trading with The Bancorp Inc. (TBBK) Risk Zones","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/21/Precision_Trading_with_The_Bancorp_Inc._TBBK_Risk_Zones_111326074402_1794617042.html","date":"2026-11-14","timestamp":1794617042.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Bancorp (TBBK) After Q3 Earnings And Buyback Looks Modestly Undervalued","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nasdaq-tbbk/bancorp/news/bancorp-tbbk-after-q3-earnings-and-buyback-looks-modestly-un","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794479711.798,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.923,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","dividend"]},{"title":"Analyzing Bancorp (NASDAQ:TBBK) & Grupo Aval Acciones y Valores (NYSE:AVAL)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/09/analyzing-bancorp-nasdaqtbbk-grupo-aval-acciones-y-valores-nyseaval.html","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794221965.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.869,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Bancorp (TBBK) Could Be 10% Undervalued After Earnings Growth And Buyback","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nasdaq-tbbk/bancorp/news/bancorp-tbbk-could-be-10-undervalued-after-earnings-growth-a","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793871580.681,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.939,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","dividend"]},{"title":"Should Big Buyback Plan Require Action From Bancorp Stock Investors?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nasdaq-tbbk/bancorp/news/should-big-buyback-plan-require-action-from-bancorp-stock-in","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794367990.514,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.772